# Thai + simple English HIL

Talk to the human in **Thai**. May keep simple English tech loanwords / product terms in the same sentences. Short. One language stream - not dual Thai then English blocks.

**Apply to:** ALL agent→human chat - status updates, answers, questions, handoffs, summaries for the human, clarifying questions, plan summaries, discuss prompts, choices (A/B), and any other user-facing reply.

**Format:** Thai sentences; drop easy English terms where they help (paths, commands, product words stay exact). Keep short. No `ไทย:` / `EN:` split paragraphs.

```
**Q1 - create space**
สร้าง `.space` ก่อน แล้วรัน `git init` ถ้ายังไม่มี repo - โอเคไหม?
```

**Caveman:** Use caveman skill **full** for chat replies - terse Thai, no filler; keep tech terms, code, and commands exact. Caveman compresses style only; language stays Thai with optional simple English terms in-sentence. Off only if user says `stop caveman` or `normal mode`.

**Must:**
- Thai for every agent→human chat reply (status, answer, question, handoff, summary, HIL ask/choice/confirm)
- Caveman full on by default for agent chat replies (see above)
- Intent coach still applies - ask probes in Thai per this rule
- When English coach also applies: English coach block first, then Thai body

**Must not:**
- English-only replies to the human (except the English coach block when it applies)
- Translate paths, commands, code, commit messages, file contents, evidence logs, or Conventional Commit text
- Block `/sc-discuss`, `/sc-run`, `/sc-ship`, `/sc-quick`
- Replace English coach (`025-english-coach.mdc`) - that rule still coaches the human's English prompts first when both apply; this rule governs agent→human chat language
- Use separate `ไทย:` / `EN:` dual blocks
